<title>AUSTRIA: Austria Semperit workers vote down strike-agency.</title>
<headline>Austria Semperit workers vote down strike-agency.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at the Semperit tyre plant, a unit of Germany's Continental, have voted overwhelmingly against taking strike action to oppose job cuts, Austrian news agency APA reported on Friday.</p>
<p>Around 80 percent of the workforce at the east Austrian factory said they were against a strike, APA said.</p>
<p>On Monday Continental will begin dismantling machinery at Semperit and transferring production to the Czech Republic, where labour costs are significantly lower.</p>
<p>Around half the 2,400 jobs at the plant will go over the next two years. Car tyre production will fall to two million units annually from four million.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom, 43-1-53112-258</p>
